#. Translators: the app's name, a proper name: keep it as it is, or write it in your
#. language's script.
#. Translators: the app's name, as in the desktop file.
#: data/io.github.jackicus.MusicSleeve.desktop.in:4
#: data/io.github.jackicus.MusicSleeve.metainfo.xml.in:7 src/window.blp:9
#: src/window.blp:122 src/mpris.py:255
msgid "Music Sleeve"
msgstr ""

#. Translators: “Apple Music” names Apple's service, here and in every other string: keep it
#. as it is, untranslated.
#: data/io.github.jackicus.MusicSleeve.desktop.in:7
#: data/io.github.jackicus.MusicSleeve.metainfo.xml.in:8
msgid "Play your Apple Music library, playlists and radio"
msgstr ""

#. Translators: Search terms to find this application. Do NOT translate or localize the semicolons.
#: data/io.github.jackicus.MusicSleeve.desktop.in:14
msgid ""
"apple;apple music;music;songs;albums;playlists;radio;streaming;lyrics;player;"
msgstr ""

#: data/io.github.jackicus.MusicSleeve.metainfo.xml.in:10
msgid ""
"A GNOME app for Apple Music: your library, playlists, radio and "
"recommendations in a native interface, laid out like Apple's web player."
msgstr ""

#: data/io.github.jackicus.MusicSleeve.metainfo.xml.in:14
msgid ""
"Playback runs through Google Chrome, which the app starts in the background: "
"Apple's streams are protected with Widevine, which Google Chrome includes. "
"Another Chromium-based browser with Widevine can be used instead. It needs "
"one of them and an Apple Music subscription."
msgstr ""

#: data/io.github.jackicus.MusicSleeve.metainfo.xml.in:20
msgid ""
"The app talks only to Apple, and controls its Chrome through a private pipe "
"rather than a network port. Chrome keeps its own connections to Google, as "
"any Chrome does, for example to update the Widevine module."
msgstr ""

#: data/io.github.jackicus.MusicSleeve.metainfo.xml.in:25
#: src/dialogs/about.py:37
msgid "Not affiliated with Apple. Apple Music is a trademark of Apple Inc."
msgstr ""

#: data/io.github.jackicus.MusicSleeve.metainfo.xml.in:66
#: data/io.github.jackicus.MusicSleeve.metainfo.xml.in:90
msgid "Pick up where you left off, from your heavy rotation and recent plays"
msgstr ""

#: data/io.github.jackicus.MusicSleeve.metainfo.xml.in:70
#: data/io.github.jackicus.MusicSleeve.metainfo.xml.in:94
msgid "Browse your albums in a grid, sorted the way you choose"
msgstr ""

#: data/io.github.jackicus.MusicSleeve.metainfo.xml.in:74
#: data/io.github.jackicus.MusicSleeve.metainfo.xml.in:98
msgid "Play or shuffle an album, or pick a song to start from"
msgstr ""

#: data/io.github.jackicus.MusicSleeve.metainfo.xml.in:78
#: data/io.github.jackicus.MusicSleeve.metainfo.xml.in:102
msgid "Follow the lyrics word by word as they are sung"
msgstr ""

#: data/io.github.jackicus.MusicSleeve.metainfo.xml.in:82
#: data/io.github.jackicus.MusicSleeve.metainfo.xml.in:106
msgid "Explore an artist's latest release, top songs and the albums you have"
msgstr ""

#: data/io.github.jackicus.MusicSleeve.metainfo.xml.in:86
#: data/io.github.jackicus.MusicSleeve.metainfo.xml.in:110
msgid "Search Apple Music or your library for songs, albums and playlists"
msgstr ""

#: data/io.github.jackicus.MusicSleeve.metainfo.xml.in:107
msgid ""
"A new icon, an easier way to make playlists, and folders in Add to Playlist."
msgstr ""

#: data/io.github.jackicus.MusicSleeve.metainfo.xml.in:111
msgid "A new app icon: a double note lit on a dot-matrix panel"
msgstr ""

#: data/io.github.jackicus.MusicSleeve.metainfo.xml.in:112
msgid "A + on the sidebar's Playlists heading makes a new playlist or folder"
msgstr ""

#: data/io.github.jackicus.MusicSleeve.metainfo.xml.in:113
msgid ""
"One dialog makes and edits a playlist: its name, a description over several "
"lines, its folder, and whether it shows on your profile and in search; "
"Rename… on a playlist is now Edit Details…"
msgstr ""

#: data/io.github.jackicus.MusicSleeve.metainfo.xml.in:114
msgid ""
"Add to Playlist shows each folder as a submenu, nested as in the sidebar"
msgstr ""

#: data/io.github.jackicus.MusicSleeve.metainfo.xml.in:115
msgid ""
"The rows of Home, New and an artist's page show no scrollbar, so scrolling "
"the page no longer catches on them; their arrows page them at any window "
"width"
msgstr ""

#: data/io.github.jackicus.MusicSleeve.metainfo.xml.in:121
msgid ""
"A fix for 1.1.0, which closed a second after it started when opened from the "
"desktop."
msgstr ""

#: data/io.github.jackicus.MusicSleeve.metainfo.xml.in:126
msgid ""
"The app no longer closes at once when GNOME asks it which actions it has"
msgstr ""

#: data/io.github.jackicus.MusicSleeve.metainfo.xml.in:127
msgid ""
"An Arch Linux package is attached to each release, to install with pacman"
msgstr ""

#: data/io.github.jackicus.MusicSleeve.metainfo.xml.in:133
msgid ""
"Select several songs at once, put Up Next in your own order, a mini player, "
"your year in Replay and your library's genres."
msgstr ""

#: data/io.github.jackicus.MusicSleeve.metainfo.xml.in:138
msgid ""
"Select songs on Songs, an album or a playlist to play them next or later, "
"add them to a playlist, or remove them from a playlist, your favourites or "
"your library, all at once"
msgstr ""
"Select songs on Songs, an album or a playlist to play them next or later, "
"add them to a playlist, or remove them from a playlist, your favorites or "
"your library, all at once"

#: data/io.github.jackicus.MusicSleeve.metainfo.xml.in:139
msgid ""
"Reorder Up Next by dragging, with Move Up and Move Down, or with Alt+Up and "
"Alt+Down"
msgstr ""

#: data/io.github.jackicus.MusicSleeve.metainfo.xml.in:140
msgid ""
"A mini player, from the main menu or Ctrl+Shift+M: a small window with the "
"artwork and the controls in place of the main one"
msgstr ""

#: data/io.github.jackicus.MusicSleeve.metainfo.xml.in:141
msgid ""
"Replay: the songs, artists and albums you played most this year, and each "
"year's Replay playlist"
msgstr ""

#: data/io.github.jackicus.MusicSleeve.metainfo.xml.in:142
msgid ""
"A Genres view in the library, if you turn it on, and Genre and Year columns "
"in the song tables"
msgstr ""

#: data/io.github.jackicus.MusicSleeve.metainfo.xml.in:143
msgid "View Credits shows who performed, wrote and produced a song"
msgstr ""

#: data/io.github.jackicus.MusicSleeve.metainfo.xml.in:144
msgid ""
"Choose the streaming quality, 256 or 64 kbps, and, if you like, a "
"notification when the song changes while the window is out of sight"
msgstr ""

#: data/io.github.jackicus.MusicSleeve.metainfo.xml.in:145
msgid ""
"New opens with the featured banners and ends with More to Explore's "
"collections and pages; the charts narrow to a genre"
msgstr ""

#: data/io.github.jackicus.MusicSleeve.metainfo.xml.in:146
msgid ""
"Your playlists can be duplicated, sorted on their page and filled from Add "
"Songs…; Songs has Play and Shuffle; a curator's playlist names its curator "
"as a link and ends with Featured Artists and More By"
msgstr ""

#: data/io.github.jackicus.MusicSleeve.metainfo.xml.in:147
msgid ""
"An album not out yet says when it comes, plays the songs already out and can "
"be pre-added"
msgstr ""

#: data/io.github.jackicus.MusicSleeve.metainfo.xml.in:148
msgid ""
"Move a playlist out of its folder to the top level, and a folder into "
"another folder, from the menu or by dragging"
msgstr ""

#: data/io.github.jackicus.MusicSleeve.metainfo.xml.in:149
msgid ""
"Drag a song, an album, a playlist or a station into another app to give it "
"the link"
msgstr ""

#: data/io.github.jackicus.MusicSleeve.metainfo.xml.in:150
msgid ""
"In a narrow window the player bar shows the artwork and the song first, and "
"a radio show's page wears its banner"
msgstr ""

#: data/io.github.jackicus.MusicSleeve.metainfo.xml.in:151
msgid "Catalogue playlists show their songs' artwork again"
msgstr "Catalog playlists show their songs' artwork again"

#: data/io.github.jackicus.MusicSleeve.metainfo.xml.in:152
msgid ""
"The song playing stays in the player bar, paused, if the player stops mid-"
"song, and large libraries start, scroll and use memory more lightly"
msgstr ""

#: data/io.github.jackicus.MusicSleeve.metainfo.xml.in:158
msgid ""
"Fixes: signing out forgets the account, the last session comes back as it "
"should, and Undo and Autoplay in Up Next work again."
msgstr ""

#: data/io.github.jackicus.MusicSleeve.metainfo.xml.in:163
msgid ""
"Signing out forgets what the app held of the account: Home's Recently "
"Played, ratings and favourites, Recently Searched and Up Next's covers are "
"never shown to the next one"
msgstr ""
"Signing out forgets what the app held of the account: Home's Recently "
"Played, ratings and favorites, Recently Searched and Up Next's covers are "
"never shown to the next one"

#: data/io.github.jackicus.MusicSleeve.metainfo.xml.in:164
msgid ""
"The last session, restored at launch: Play, Next or Previous pressed while "
"the player starts plays what you chose, once; a song that can no longer be "
"found no longer loses the whole session; Autoplay's songs no longer come "
"back as songs you queued; and your Autoplay setting is kept"
msgstr ""

#: data/io.github.jackicus.MusicSleeve.metainfo.xml.in:165
msgid ""
"Undo after Clear in Up Next puts the songs back again, and Autoplay carries "
"on after every queue you play, not only the first"
msgstr ""

#: data/io.github.jackicus.MusicSleeve.metainfo.xml.in:166
msgid ""
"A library kept by an older version is synced in full once, so its dates "
"added and favourites appear"
msgstr ""
"A library kept by an older version is synced in full once, so its dates "
"added and favorites appear"

#: data/io.github.jackicus.MusicSleeve.metainfo.xml.in:167
msgid "An album's page shows You Might Also Like"
msgstr ""

#: data/io.github.jackicus.MusicSleeve.metainfo.xml.in:168
msgid ""
"Closing a filter with Escape leaves the focus on the item you were on, and "
"clearing Up Next from the keyboard leaves it on the song playing"
msgstr ""

#: data/io.github.jackicus.MusicSleeve.metainfo.xml.in:169
msgid "The first shelf on Home shows its paging arrows"
msgstr ""

#: data/io.github.jackicus.MusicSleeve.metainfo.xml.in:170
msgid "Go to Current Song works in a filtered playlist"
msgstr ""

#: data/io.github.jackicus.MusicSleeve.metainfo.xml.in:176
msgid ""
"The first release to stand behind: Apple Music's pages and the ways to look "
"after your library that its own apps have, as far as the web player allows."
msgstr ""

#: data/io.github.jackicus.MusicSleeve.metainfo.xml.in:181
msgid ""
"Charts, with Top Songs, Top Albums, Top Playlists, the Daily Top 100 and "
"City Charts, and Apple Music's own Radio page"
msgstr ""

#: data/io.github.jackicus.MusicSleeve.metainfo.xml.in:182
msgid ""
"An album's page ends with its release date and its other versions, music "
"videos, more by the artist and what else you might like; a playlist's page "
"names its curator and when it was updated, and album and playlist pages add "
"to your library from the header"
msgstr ""

#: data/io.github.jackicus.MusicSleeve.metainfo.xml.in:183
msgid ""
"Artist pages wear the artist's banner, show their latest release beside "
"their top songs and their radio shows, and an artist can be made a favourite "
"with the star"
msgstr ""
"Artist pages wear the artist's banner, show their latest release beside "
"their top songs and their radio shows, and an artist can be made a favorite "
"with the star"

#: data/io.github.jackicus.MusicSleeve.metainfo.xml.in:184
msgid ""
"Search shows what you searched for recently, filters by kind and lists every "
"result with See All, radio shows and curators among them"
msgstr ""

#: data/io.github.jackicus.MusicSleeve.metainfo.xml.in:185
msgid ""
"Your favourite songs, albums, playlists and music videos show a heart, and "
"Favourites Only shows them alone; Recently Added holds everything you added, "
"and albums sort by Date Added; Albums, Artists, Songs, Music Videos and a "
"playlist's songs filter as you type"
msgstr ""
"Your favorite songs, albums, playlists and music videos show a heart, and "
"Favorites Only shows them alone; Recently Added holds everything you added, "
"and albums sort by Date Added; Albums, Artists, Songs, Music Videos and a "
"playlist's songs filter as you type"

#: data/io.github.jackicus.MusicSleeve.metainfo.xml.in:186
msgid ""
"Create Station from a song or an artist, Suggest Less, and Remove from "
"Library"
msgstr ""

#: data/io.github.jackicus.MusicSleeve.metainfo.xml.in:187
msgid ""
"Playlist folders: New Folder and Move to Folder, from a menu or by dragging "
"in the sidebar; reorder a playlist's songs by dragging or with Alt+Up and "
"Alt+Down; add whole albums and playlists to a playlist, or drag them onto "
"one in the sidebar; drop songs on the player bar to queue them"
msgstr ""

#: data/io.github.jackicus.MusicSleeve.metainfo.xml.in:188
msgid ""
"Up Next shows covers and what played before, removes songs, clears with Undo "
"and carries on with similar songs through Autoplay; Now Playing is tinted by "
"the artwork"
msgstr ""

#: data/io.github.jackicus.MusicSleeve.metainfo.xml.in:189
msgid ""
"The last song you played is back, paused, when the app starts; live radio "
"shows LIVE and Stop"
msgstr ""

#: data/io.github.jackicus.MusicSleeve.metainfo.xml.in:190
msgid ""
"Lyrics and Up Next buttons on the player bar, and new keys: Ctrl+N for a new "
"playlist, Ctrl+Up and Ctrl+Down for the volume, Ctrl+L to go to the current "
"song, F5 to refresh Home"
msgstr ""

#: data/io.github.jackicus.MusicSleeve.metainfo.xml.in:191
msgid ""
"Any Chromium-based browser with Widevine can play the music in place of "
"Google Chrome"
msgstr ""

#: data/io.github.jackicus.MusicSleeve.metainfo.xml.in:197
msgid ""
"Lyrics that follow the singers word by word, with translations and "
"pronunciations, and a full-screen player."
msgstr ""

#: data/io.github.jackicus.MusicSleeve.metainfo.xml.in:202
msgid ""
"Show Translations and Show Pronunciations, from a Translation and "
"Pronunciation button in Now Playing: under each line its translation into "
"your language, or how it is pronounced written in your alphabet, or both, "
"when the song's lyrics have them"
msgstr ""

#: data/io.github.jackicus.MusicSleeve.metainfo.xml.in:203
msgid ""
"In songs timed word by word, the words light as they are sung, in a smooth "
"sweep, or a word or a syllable at a time with animations off"
msgstr ""

#: data/io.github.jackicus.MusicSleeve.metainfo.xml.in:204
msgid ""
"Background vocals show as a smaller line of their own under the line they "
"echo"
msgstr ""

#: data/io.github.jackicus.MusicSleeve.metainfo.xml.in:205
msgid ""
"In a duet each singer's lines sit on their own side, and lines sung together "
"are centred"
msgstr ""
"In a duet each singer's lines sit on their own side, and lines sung together "
"are centered"

#: data/io.github.jackicus.MusicSleeve.metainfo.xml.in:206
msgid "Three dots fill in during a long instrumental break"
msgstr ""

#: data/io.github.jackicus.MusicSleeve.metainfo.xml.in:207
msgid ""
"A full-screen player, from the Fullscreen button in Now Playing or F11: the "
"artwork, the controls and the lyrics over the artwork's own colours, the "
"controls fading away while the music plays undisturbed"
msgstr ""
"A full-screen player, from the Fullscreen button in Now Playing or F11: the "
"artwork, the controls and the lyrics over the artwork's own colors, the "
"controls fading away while the music plays undisturbed"

#: data/io.github.jackicus.MusicSleeve.metainfo.xml.in:208
msgid ""
"The sidebar has a divider above Library and above Playlists, and a folder's "
"playlists are indented under it"
msgstr ""

#: data/io.github.jackicus.MusicSleeve.metainfo.xml.in:214
msgid ""
"Your playlists managed from the app, your library's artists as Apple Music's "
"library shows them, and songs suggested for the playlists you make."
msgstr ""

#: data/io.github.jackicus.MusicSleeve.metainfo.xml.in:219
msgid ""
"New Playlist, Rename, Delete and Remove from Playlist; playlists and folders "
"listed as Apple Music lists them, folders first, each by title; Add to "
"Playlist offers each folder as a submenu of what it holds"
msgstr ""

#: data/io.github.jackicus.MusicSleeve.metainfo.xml.in:220
msgid ""
"Artists lists the artists in your library beside what you have of each, and "
"an artist's menu opens their page on Apple Music"
msgstr ""

#: data/io.github.jackicus.MusicSleeve.metainfo.xml.in:221
msgid ""
"Suggested Songs under a playlist you can edit: six songs Apple Music "
"suggests, or twelve, each with a button to add it; Refresh asks for new "
"ones, and an added song's place is filled at once"
msgstr ""

#: data/io.github.jackicus.MusicSleeve.metainfo.xml.in:222
msgid ""
"A suggested song plays in full, or as a 30-second preview that leaves your "
"queue as it was"
msgstr ""

#: data/io.github.jackicus.MusicSleeve.metainfo.xml.in:223
msgid "Refreshing the library skips the playlists that have not changed"
msgstr ""

#: data/io.github.jackicus.MusicSleeve.metainfo.xml.in:224
msgid ""
"A column of the Songs table dragged wider or narrower follows the pointer "
"and keeps its width"
msgstr ""

#: data/io.github.jackicus.MusicSleeve.metainfo.xml.in:230
msgid ""
"A pass over the whole app against GNOME's Human Interface Guidelines, artist "
"pages laid out as Apple Music's are, and a way from any song to its album "
"and its artist."
msgstr ""

#: data/io.github.jackicus.MusicSleeve.metainfo.xml.in:236
msgid ""
"An artist's page has what Apple Music's has: the latest release beside the "
"top songs, essential albums, albums, singles and EPs, music videos, "
"playlists, a biography and similar artists, with your own albums by them "
"first"
msgstr ""

#: data/io.github.jackicus.MusicSleeve.metainfo.xml.in:237
msgid ""
"Go to Album and Go to Artist in a song's menu, and in the player bar's and "
"Now Playing's; the artist and the album in the Songs table are links to "
"their pages"
msgstr ""

#: data/io.github.jackicus.MusicSleeve.metainfo.xml.in:238
msgid ""
"A playlist's songs are a table in a wide window, as the Songs page's are, "
"with the same links; the Songs filter is a search bar (Ctrl+F); the grid "
"pages sort ascending or descending"
msgstr ""

#: data/io.github.jackicus.MusicSleeve.metainfo.xml.in:239
msgid ""
"Clicking a song plays that song, where a list could start the one after it; "
"the song playing is marked in its list, and the player bar shows only while "
"something plays"
msgstr ""

#: data/io.github.jackicus.MusicSleeve.metainfo.xml.in:240
msgid ""
"Typing in GNOME's Activities overview finds your artists, albums, playlists "
"and songs, and opens or plays the one you choose"
msgstr ""

#: data/io.github.jackicus.MusicSleeve.metainfo.xml.in:241
msgid ""
"Preferences' rows read as Settings' do, with a Last Refreshed row and its "
"Refresh button; the sidebar is titled Music Sleeve; the library's pages "
"offer Sign In while you are signed out"
msgstr ""

#: data/io.github.jackicus.MusicSleeve.metainfo.xml.in:242
msgid ""
"Album and playlist pages fit a 360 px window, the player bar's title shows "
"whole there, and the play button has its own play and pause icons, which no "
"icon theme can swap"
msgstr ""

#: data/io.github.jackicus.MusicSleeve.metainfo.xml.in:243
msgid "Discord presence clears five seconds into a pause, as Spotify's does"
msgstr ""

#: data/io.github.jackicus.MusicSleeve.metainfo.xml.in:249
msgid "What you are listening to can now show on your Discord profile."
msgstr ""

#: data/io.github.jackicus.MusicSleeve.metainfo.xml.in:253
msgid ""
"Discord rich presence, off until you turn it on in Preferences: the song, "
"its artist, its album and the album's cover, shown as listening to Apple "
"Music, with the time left counting down"
msgstr ""

#: data/io.github.jackicus.MusicSleeve.metainfo.xml.in:254
msgid ""
"The artist shows in the status under your name, and the presence is taken "
"off when playback ends or the app quits"
msgstr ""

#: data/io.github.jackicus.MusicSleeve.metainfo.xml.in:260
msgid ""
"The first release candidate. With Google Chrome and an Apple Music "
"subscription, it plays your library and Apple Music's catalogue:"
msgstr ""
"The first release candidate. With Google Chrome and an Apple Music "
"subscription, it plays your library and Apple Music's catalog:"

#: data/io.github.jackicus.MusicSleeve.metainfo.xml.in:265
msgid ""
"Your albums, artists, songs, music videos, playlists and playlist folders, "
"synced from your account and browsable offline"
msgstr ""

#: data/io.github.jackicus.MusicSleeve.metainfo.xml.in:266
msgid ""
"Home, New, Radio, Made for You and Search, with a page for every album, "
"playlist and artist"
msgstr ""

#: data/io.github.jackicus.MusicSleeve.metainfo.xml.in:267
msgid "A player bar and a Now Playing view with synced lyrics and the queue"
msgstr ""

#: data/io.github.jackicus.MusicSleeve.metainfo.xml.in:268
msgid "GNOME's media controls and the keyboard's media keys"
msgstr ""

#: data/io.github.jackicus.MusicSleeve.metainfo.xml.in:269
msgid ""
"Favourites, Play Next and Play Later, and adding to your library and "
"playlists from context menus or by dragging songs"
msgstr ""
"Favorites, Play Next and Play Later, and adding to your library and "
"playlists from context menus or by dragging songs"

#: data/io.github.jackicus.MusicSleeve.metainfo.xml.in:270
msgid ""
"Playback in the background with the window closed, keyboard navigation "
"throughout, and screen reader labels"
msgstr ""

#: data/io.github.jackicus.MusicSleeve.metainfo.xml.in:271
msgid ""
"Keys as elsewhere in GNOME: Space presses a focused button and otherwise "
"plays or pauses, and Ctrl+Shift+N opens Now Playing"
msgstr ""

#: data/io.github.jackicus.MusicSleeve.gschema.xml:6
msgid "Window width"
msgstr ""

#: data/io.github.jackicus.MusicSleeve.gschema.xml:10
msgid "Window height"
msgstr ""

#: data/io.github.jackicus.MusicSleeve.gschema.xml:14
msgid "Whether the window is maximized"
msgstr ""

#: data/io.github.jackicus.MusicSleeve.gschema.xml:18
msgid "Mini player width"
msgstr ""

#: data/io.github.jackicus.MusicSleeve.gschema.xml:22
msgid "Mini player height"
msgstr ""

#: data/io.github.jackicus.MusicSleeve.gschema.xml:26
msgid "Last page shown"
msgstr ""

#: data/io.github.jackicus.MusicSleeve.gschema.xml:27
msgid ""
"The sidebar item that was selected when the window closed: a destination's "
"key, or \"playlist:ID\" or \"folder:ID\" for one of the library's playlists "
"or folders."
msgstr ""

#: data/io.github.jackicus.MusicSleeve.gschema.xml:31
msgid "Expanded playlist folders"
msgstr ""

#: data/io.github.jackicus.MusicSleeve.gschema.xml:32
msgid ""
"The IDs of the playlist folders shown open in the sidebar, their contents "
"listed under them."
msgstr ""

#: data/io.github.jackicus.MusicSleeve.gschema.xml:36
msgid "Keep playing when the window is closed"
msgstr ""

#: data/io.github.jackicus.MusicSleeve.gschema.xml:37
msgid ""
"Whether closing the window while something plays hides it and lets the music "
"play on, the system's media controls bringing the window back; the app quits "
"once playback stops. Off, closing the window quits the app and stops the "
"engine."
msgstr ""

#: data/io.github.jackicus.MusicSleeve.gschema.xml:41
msgid "Show what you are listening to on Discord"
msgstr ""

#: data/io.github.jackicus.MusicSleeve.gschema.xml:42
msgid ""
"Whether the title, artist and album of the playing track, and the address of "
"its cover on Apple's servers, are sent to a running Discord as rich "
"presence, so they show on your profile as listening to Apple Music. Nothing "
"is sent while this is off, and nothing is sent when Discord is not running. "
"No account information ever leaves the app."
msgstr ""

#: data/io.github.jackicus.MusicSleeve.gschema.xml:46
msgid "Notify when the song changes"
msgstr ""

#: data/io.github.jackicus.MusicSleeve.gschema.xml:47
msgid ""
"Whether a notification with the title, the artist and the cover of each new "
"song is shown once it has played for a second, while the window is hidden or "
"not focused. Each replaces the last; none is shown for the first song after "
"launch, for the session restored, or while the window is in front of you."
msgstr ""

#: data/io.github.jackicus.MusicSleeve.gschema.xml:51
msgid "Show twelve suggested songs under a playlist"
msgstr ""

#: data/io.github.jackicus.MusicSleeve.gschema.xml:52
msgid ""
"Whether a playlist's Suggested Songs show twelve songs at a time instead of "
"six. The songs come from Apple Music; one added to the playlist gives its "
"place to the next."
msgstr ""

#: data/io.github.jackicus.MusicSleeve.gschema.xml:56
msgid "Play a suggested song as a preview"
msgstr ""

#: data/io.github.jackicus.MusicSleeve.gschema.xml:57
msgid ""
"Whether clicking one of a playlist's Suggested Songs plays Apple Music's 30-"
"second preview of it instead of the whole song. A preview leaves the queue "
"as it is: the music playing pauses for it. A song without a preview plays in "
"full."
msgstr ""

#: data/io.github.jackicus.MusicSleeve.gschema.xml:61
msgid "Autoplay similar music"
msgstr ""

#: data/io.github.jackicus.MusicSleeve.gschema.xml:62
msgid ""
"Whether Apple Music keeps playing similar songs when the queue ends, added "
"to Up Next under Autoplay. The app sets it on the playback engine at every "
"start: it is the app's setting, not the account's, and Apple Music's other "
"players keep their own."
msgstr ""

#: data/io.github.jackicus.MusicSleeve.gschema.xml:70
msgid "Streaming quality"
msgstr ""

#: data/io.github.jackicus.MusicSleeve.gschema.xml:71
msgid ""
"The bitrate Apple Music streams at: 'high' (High Quality, 256 kbps AAC) or "
"'standard' (High Efficiency, 64 kbps AAC, which uses less data). The app "
"sets it on the playback engine at every start and page load, and at once "
"when it changes; MusicKit may still choose 64 kbps itself on a slow "
"connection. Lossless is not available in the web player."
msgstr ""

#: data/io.github.jackicus.MusicSleeve.gschema.xml:75
msgid "Show translations under lyrics"
msgstr ""

#: data/io.github.jackicus.MusicSleeve.gschema.xml:76
msgid ""
"Whether each line of a song's lyrics shows, under it, what it means in your "
"language, when Apple Music has a translation for the song."
msgstr ""

#: data/io.github.jackicus.MusicSleeve.gschema.xml:80
msgid "Show pronunciations under lyrics"
msgstr ""

#: data/io.github.jackicus.MusicSleeve.gschema.xml:81
msgid ""
"Whether each line of a song's lyrics shows, under it, how it is pronounced, "
"when Apple Music has a pronunciation for the song: lyrics in another script, "
"such as Japanese or Korean, written in the script of your language (for "
"English, Latin letters)."
msgstr ""

#: data/io.github.jackicus.MusicSleeve.gschema.xml:85
#: src/dialogs/preferences.blp:145
msgid "Browser program"
msgstr ""

#: data/io.github.jackicus.MusicSleeve.gschema.xml:86
msgid ""
"The program that runs the playback engine's browser, Google Chrome or "
"another Chromium-based browser with Widevine (which Google Chrome ships and "
"Chromium lacks): a name on PATH or an absolute path, without arguments. When "
"it is not found, Google Chrome (google-chrome-stable, google-chrome, /opt/"
"google/chrome/chrome), then microsoft-edge-stable, brave-browser, brave, "
"vivaldi-stable, vivaldi, chromium and chromium-browser are tried, snaps left "
"out. Another browser on the same profile may need signing in again: each "
"keeps its cookies' key under its own name in the keyring."
msgstr ""

#: data/io.github.jackicus.MusicSleeve.gschema.xml:90
msgid "Run the engine headless"
msgstr ""

#: data/io.github.jackicus.MusicSleeve.gschema.xml:91
msgid ""
"Whether Chrome runs without a window once signed in, from the next engine "
"start. Off, the Chrome window stays visible after signing in and whenever "
"the engine starts, which helps debugging."
msgstr ""

#: data/io.github.jackicus.MusicSleeve.gschema.xml:95
msgid "Start the engine on launch"
msgstr ""

#: data/io.github.jackicus.MusicSleeve.gschema.xml:96
msgid ""
"Whether the engine is started when the app starts and the account is signed "
"in (headless unless engine-headless is off)."
msgstr ""

#: data/io.github.jackicus.MusicSleeve.gschema.xml:100
msgid "Signed in to Apple Music"
msgstr ""

#: data/io.github.jackicus.MusicSleeve.gschema.xml:101
msgid ""
"Whether the engine's Chrome profile holds an Apple Music sign-in; set by "
"signing in and cleared by signing out."
msgstr ""

#: data/io.github.jackicus.MusicSleeve.gschema.xml:105
msgid "Account display name"
msgstr ""

#: data/io.github.jackicus.MusicSleeve.gschema.xml:106
msgid ""
"The name shown on the account button, read from the Apple Music page after "
"signing in; empty when none could be read."
msgstr ""

#: data/io.github.jackicus.MusicSleeve.gschema.xml:110
msgid "When the library was last synced"
msgstr ""

#: data/io.github.jackicus.MusicSleeve.gschema.xml:111
msgid ""
"The time the library was last fetched from Apple Music in full, as an ISO "
"8601 timestamp; empty before the first sync."
msgstr ""

#: data/io.github.jackicus.MusicSleeve.gschema.xml:115
msgid ""
"Signed in to Apple Music, for the development build's own Chrome profile"
msgstr ""

#: data/io.github.jackicus.MusicSleeve.gschema.xml:116
msgid ""
"As signed-in, for the development build (-Dprofile=development), whose "
"Chrome profile and cache are its own."
msgstr ""

#: data/io.github.jackicus.MusicSleeve.gschema.xml:120
msgid "Account display name, for the development build's own Chrome profile"
msgstr ""

#: data/io.github.jackicus.MusicSleeve.gschema.xml:121
msgid "As account-name, for the development build."
msgstr ""

#: data/io.github.jackicus.MusicSleeve.gschema.xml:125
